      "io.title": "International Organizations",
      "io.subtitle": "Grove Between Stars Calendar, Year 5501",
      "io.statLabel": "Total Disclosed Organizations",
      "io.footnote": "* Data compiled by the Stargazer Tower Organization's Diplomatic Research Division · Only the minimum basic intelligence is disclosed",
      "io.col.org": "Organization",
      "io.col.hq": "Headquarters",
      "io.col.members": "Members",
      "io.col.desc": "Summary",
      "io.org1.name": "<br>Union of Non-Centralized Nations",
      "io.org1.hq": "<br>Star-Ring Segment 12",
      "io.org1.desc": "Initiated by the Deep Sea Alliance, its original aim was to provide collective political endorsement to non-centralized nations in an age when the tide of authoritarianism swept across the Grove Between Stars. Its core position is to counter ideological homogenization with institutional diversity, holding that no single civilization has the right to export a model of governance to others in the name of 'progress' or 'efficiency.' Internal disagreements among its members keep widening—some have, in substance, already slid toward the very direction it nominally opposes.",
      "io.org2.name": "<br>Grove Between Stars Community of Shared Destiny",
      "io.org2.hq": "<br>Grace City",
      "io.org2.desc": "Founded as a direct response to the Union of Non-Centralized Nations, with the Grace Empire at its core, it holds that the civilizations of the Grove Between Stars should transcend institutional differences and move toward unity in the face of a shared destiny. Internally it strengthens the political cohesion of its members through a collectivist narrative; externally it characterizes pluralistic coexistence as the root of inefficiency and security risk. In an age of extraordinarily advanced productive forces, it proves one thing: a dictatorship, wrapped in a grand enough narrative, can still maintain considerable legitimacy on every kind of international stage.",
      "io.org3.name": "<br>Tear-Worship Brotherhood",
      "io.org3.hq": "<br>Sun-Moon-Starlight Holy Land",
      "io.org3.desc": "Taking Tear-Worship faith as the sole criterion for admission, it coalesced spontaneously from the theocratic nations of the Sun-Moon-Star Continent, and is one of the oldest religious international organizations in the history of the Grove Between Stars. Its core position is that the Holy-Writ Legal System is universal, and that any civilization's 'true perfection' on the spiritual plane must be achieved through Tear-Worship doctrine. A high degree of internal unity and an equal degree of external exclusivity make it, in diplomatic settings, always a whole that is hard to break apart and hard to ignore.",
      "io.org4.name": "<br>Pact of the Unyielding",
      "io.org4.hq": "<br>Open-Sea Port",
      "io.org4.desc": "Composed of the nations of the Ascension Continent that espouse industrialism and the supremacy of productive force, it seeks to maintain an independent third position between the polar opposition of the Union of Non-Centralized Nations and the Grove Between Stars Community of Shared Destiny. Its core position is to treat economic strength and technological capacity as the sole legitimate source of a nation's voice, refusing to take sides on ideological labels. Yet this organizational logic, which treats the populace as a means rather than an end, in practice often places it nearer to authoritarianism than it openly admits.",
      "io.org5.name": "<br>Four-Nation Bloc (Barrier Alliance)",
      "io.org5.hq": "<br>Deepwinter City",
      "io.org5.desc": "With the Elf Continent at its core, the Empire of AllLife Chance-Born, the United States of Deepwinter, and the Kappa Heavy Industries Group formally allied after the end of the Deepwinter War; it is at present the most highly integrated political-economic-cultural-military alliance in the Grove Between Stars. Its members keep no defenses against one another, their high-level information fully interlinked, and they speak with a unified position to the outside. While other international organizations are still discussing trust-building mechanisms, the Four-Nation Bloc has already operated for centuries—and that, in itself, is a silent political declaration.",
      "io.org6.name": "<br>South-South Accord",
      "io.org6.hq": "<br>Sky-Shattered Archipelago",
      "io.org6.desc": "Jointly initiated by the various Cloudborn nations and the nations of the Southern Alliance, its core driving force is a shared wariness of the HiveDragon's southward expansion and the infiltration of the Tear-Worship Faith. It takes economic complementarity and intelligence-sharing as its main forms of cooperation, avoiding the establishment of a formal military command structure so as to lower the political sensitivity of its members. Pragmatic, low-key, and not seeking a sense of presence—this is the style the organization deliberately maintains. Its value lies not in what it says, but in what it coordinates at the critical moment.",
      "io.org7.name": "<br>Southern Alliance",
      "io.org7.hq": "<br>Forbidden-Curse Strait Treaty City",
      "io.org7.desc": "Initiated by the Forbidden-Curse Strait Treaty City, thirty-one nations formally allied on the basis of a defense pact after the HiveDragon's third large-scale expansion. Its core logic is simple and severe: taken alone, not one member nation could maintain stability under the HiveDragon's military pressure, and unity is the only meaningful option. In the face of cruel international-political reality, it has no grand ideological claim, only a pragmatic consensus—to survive, they need one another.",
      "io.org8.name": "<br>East Coast Guardians' Organization",
      "io.org8.hq": "<br>City of the Upright",
      "io.org8.desc": "Composed of the various military nations and knightly-order nations that the eastern coast of the Grace Continent evolved into over ten thousand years, it originates in the long history of jointly resisting the HiveDragon invasion. The HiveDragon threat today no longer holds the urgency of those years, and so the organization's reason for existence has shifted from defensive need to cultural identity—a long military tradition shaped these nations' distinctive sense of honor and ethics of war, allowing them to retain a clear self-awareness even under the pressure of being integrated and absorbed by the Grace Empire. It is no longer the most crucial force against external threats, but in resisting internal assimilation, it remains effective.",
      "tt.mainTitle": "✦ Technology Tree ✦",
