      "tt.addedTag": "Supplementary",
      "bl.mainTitle": "Beliefs &amp; Philosophy",
      "bl.overviewTitle": "Overview<br>",
      "bl.overviewBody": "<p>The Grove Between Stars has seven major faith systems and six major philosophical schools, and the lines between them are not sharply drawn—most individuals are influenced by several systems over a lifetime, invoking different frameworks in different situations.</p><p>The fundamental difference between a faith system and a philosophical school is that the former offers meaning, the latter offers method. The geographic distribution of each system correlates closely with its distribution across races.</p><p>No single faith or philosophy holds absolute dominance across the planet. This is the result of the pluralistic civilizational landscape of the Grove Between Stars.</p>",
      "bl.section.beliefs": "Faith Systems",
      "bl.section.philosophy": "Philosophical Schools",
      "bl.belief.n1.name": "The Tear-Worship Faith",
      "bl.belief.n1.body": "<p>A strict monotheistic religion.</p><p>Suffering is not a path toward the divine—</p><p>suffering itself is the manifestation of the divine.</p><p>A strict system of shared welfare;</p><p>private property is regarded as sin,</p><p>collective welfare above all else.</p><p>A vanguard priesthood leads the not-yet-awakened,</p><p>and the Tear-Worship Faith,</p><p>holding to a doctrine of perpetual holy war,</p><p>presses on until the suffering of the world is wholly ended.</p>",
      "bl.belief.n2.name": "Tranquil Moonlight",
      "bl.belief.n2.body": "<p>The Grove Between Stars</p><p>cannot, on its own, produce all 130 elements.</p><p>The iron in our blood</p><p>comes from the blaze of a supernova;</p><p>the iron in our blood</p><p>is born of the dust of two colliding neutron stars.</p><p>Even the trace of copper</p><p>required witnessing the death of a white dwarf.</p><p>All living things are born of chance—</p><p>all living things are children of the stars.</p>",
      "bl.belief.n3.name": "The World-Tree Faith",
      "bl.belief.n3.body": "<p>The World Tree</p><p>pours its grace unconditionally onto every leaf;</p><p>all races, classes, and sexes</p><p>are equal as leaves.</p><p>Its temple is open to all.</p><p>Believers take the Holy Oak as their purpose,</p><p>duty-bound to cut down the world's corruption and oppression,</p><p>and to guard the health of the world.</p>",
      "bl.belief.n4.name": "The Awakened",
      "bl.belief.n4.body": "<p>Taking awakening as the soul's only path,</p><p>tempered again and again through karma and rebirth,</p><p>through the three paths of cultivation, deed, and faith</p><p>the ignorance is gradually dissolved,</p><p>until at last transcendent liberation is attained;</p><p>with a heart of mercy and oneness, all beings are nurtured,</p><p>walking together on that road</p><p>toward complete awakening.</p>",
      "bl.belief.n5.name": "Beneath the Legend",
      "bl.belief.n5.body": "<p>Only the Emperor can save all living things;</p><p>his bloodline is sacred and undying, passed through the generations.</p><p>Beyond the empire lies corrupt darkness;</p><p>want and suffering are a sacred trial,</p><p>and the end of death is the soul's eternal endurance.</p><p>Beneath the legend, there is no private inner self.</p><p>You think you are thinking—</p><p>in truth, the Emperor, borrowing your consciousness,</p><p>has confirmed its love once more.</p>",
      "bl.belief.n6.name": "The Heavenly Way",
      "bl.belief.n6.body": "<p>The Heavenly Way is the one supreme law.</p><p>The Heavenly Way sets rebirth as the soul's nurturing;</p><p>through heavenly tribulation and the path of Ascension,</p><p>one becomes one with the Heavenly Way itself.</p><p>Cause and effect are the trial of the Heavenly Way.</p><p>It worships no gods, only reveres the law;</p><p>it begs no protection, only cultivates the self.</p>",
      "bl.belief.n7.name": "Animism",
      "bl.belief.n7.body": "<p>Ancestral spirits guard the family through the rest-period,</p><p>at last merging into the land to become part of its spirit.</p><p>Consciousness is the inborn medium for sensing the will of the spirits—</p><p>presiding over purification, spirit-summoning, sacrifice, and seasonal rites,</p><p>calling forth the flow of the spirits' will with song.</p><p>Its temple is a stretch of earth.</p><p>The land has never been silent—</p><p>we have forgotten how to listen.</p>",
      "bl.philo.n1.name": "Materialism",
      "bl.philo.n1.body": "<p>Consciousness, morality, and social order</p><p>are the products of material relations, not their cause.</p><p>It looks coldly and directly at reality as it truly is,</p><p>and from this judges the oppression hidden in structures of exploitative power.</p><p>It seeks no transcendent consolation,</p><p>believes in no abstract ideal;</p><p>standing on the hardest ground,</p><p>it examines the world in order to change it—</p><p>see the structure clearly, and only then can you move it.</p>",
      "bl.philo.n2.name": "Pre-Mortalism",
      "bl.philo.n2.body": "<p>Death is the absolute end.</p><p>An afterlife, rebirth, posthumous fame—</p><p>all are illusion. Each moment</p><p>before death arrives is the only one worth giving everything to.</p><p>It takes one's own happiness and interest,</p><p>and authentic experience, as the highest standard.</p><p>The Pre-Mortalist is a thoroughly clear-eyed dweller in the present:</p><p>self-interested, authentic, within finite time,</p><p>never diminishing the quality of living for anything after death.</p>",
      "bl.philo.n3.name": "Fate-Unity Theory",
      "bl.philo.n3.body": "<p>Beyond the boundaries of reason,</p><p>the fates of all living things</p><p>are one vast web.</p><p>Every existence has its place in the structure,</p><p>every strand of fate is part of the whole.</p><p>Living things are both the bearers of fate</p><p>and its co-weavers.</p><p>Every fate</p><p>deserves to be taken seriously.</p>",
      "bl.philo.n4.name": "Pan-Rationalism",
      "bl.philo.n4.body": "<p>The world has a deep structure that reason can grasp.</p><p>Social order and moral standards should be built</p><p>through logical deduction, not tradition or gods.</p><p>It believes living things forge a civilizational contract by means of reason;</p><p>chaos is merely where reason has not yet</p><p>arrived—not the essence of the world.</p><p>The Pan-Rationalist is a calm analyst,</p><p>and a builder of order;</p><p>amid all turmoil,</p><p>firmly believing structure exists and truth is reachable.</p>",
      "bl.philo.n5.name": "Fatalism",
      "bl.philo.n5.body": "<p>The cosmos runs on</p><p>a 'Way' that exists prior to the will of any civilization,</p><p>and all things are interlinked within it.</p><p>Fate is neither the will of gods nor mere chance,</p><p>but the unfolding logic of nature itself.</p><p>The Fatalist does not struggle to change fate,</p><p>but, like a skilled sailor riding the wind,</p><p>replaces resistance with accord, anxiety with contemplation,</p><p>finding inner repose within the appointed course.</p>",
      "bl.philo.n6.name": "Praxism",
      "bl.philo.n6.body": "<p>It holds that truth</p><p>must be tested through action and experience,</p><p>and that meaning can only be created in real practice.</p><p>Set direction with reason,</p><p>correct judgment with experience, measure value by results—</p><p>a thorough actor in the present world,</p><p>believing the sole legitimacy of thought</p><p>lies in what it can change,</p><p>and that the meaning of existence</p><p>is forever in the next choice and the next act.</p>",
      "rc.mainTitle": "R A C I A L   T R A I T S",
      "rc.subtitle": "The Grove Between Stars, where many higher sapient beings coexist......",
      "rc.footnote": "* Data compiled by the Stargazer Tower Organization's Racial Research Division · Grove Between Stars Calendar, Annual Report 5501",
      "rc.col.name": "Race",
      "rc.col.bio": "Ecology / Biological Substrate",
      "rc.col.life": "Lifespan",
